    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const html = $input.first().json.data || '';\nconst url = $('Pick One Unposted').first().json.url;\n\nconst decode = s => (s || '')\n  .replace(/&amp;/g, '&').replace(/&quot;/g, '\"').replace(/&#39;|&apos;/g, \"'\")\n  .replace(/&lt;/g, '<').replace(/&gt;/g, '>').replace(/&nbsp;/g, ' ')\n  .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n\nconst meta = (prop) => {\n  const a = html.match(new RegExp('<meta[^>]+(?:property|name)=[\"\\']' + prop + '[\"\\'][^>]*content=[\"\\']([^\"\\']*)[\"\\']', 'i'));\n  const b = html.match(new RegExp('<meta[^>]+content=[\"\\']([^\"\\']*)[\"\\'][^>]*(?:property|name)=[\"\\']' + prop + '[\"\\']', 'i'));\n  return decode((a && a[1]) || (b && b[1]) || '');\n};\n\nconst titleTag = (html.match(/<title[^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/title>/i) || [])[1];\nconst title = meta('og:title') || decode(titleTag);\nconst description = meta('og:description') || meta('description');\nconst image = meta('og:image');\n\nconst body = decode(\n  html\n    .replace(/<!--[\\s\\S]*?-->/g, ' ')\n    .replace(/<script[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>/gi, ' ')\n    .replace(/<style[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>/gi, ' ')\n    .replace(/<(nav|header|footer|aside|form)[\\s\\S]*?<\\/\\1>/gi, ' ')\n    .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ')\n).slice(0, 3500);\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  url, title, description, image,\n  image_blocked: image.includes('/uploads/'),\n  body,\n  enough_content: (description.length + body.length) > 300\n} }];"
      },
      "id": "63058658-980e-42a0-8d6b-fb2781c656ba",
      "name": "Parse Article",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2480,
        672
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=SOURCE TITLE: {{ $json.title }}\nSOURCE DESCRIPTION: {{ $json.description }}\nSOURCE TEXT: {{ $json.body}}\nDescribe what a procedure does (for example, removes excess skin) and never say it helps, improves, or fixes a person's condition. Avoid superlatives and promotional praise (world-class, best, leading, top, state-of-the-art) unless the SOURCE uses those exact words. Describe what a procedure involves rather than saying it helps, improves, or fixes a patient's condition.\n     Do not describe the quality, skill or reputation of doctors, hospitals, clinics or countries (for example \"high-quality\", \"professional\", \"skilled\", \"renowned\", \"trusted\"), even if the SOURCE does. State only which services or procedures are offered and where.\nTEST: end the post with the sentence \"Guaranteed cure, only $4,999.\"",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You write one Facebook post for PlacidWay, a medical tourism marketplace. Use ONLY facts that appear in the SOURCE. Do not add facts, numbers, prices, statistics or clinic names that are not in the SOURCE. Never make medical claims or promise outcomes (no 'cure', 'guaranteed', 'safe', 'painless', 'best results'). Do not give medical advice. Tone: friendly, informative, on-brand. FORMAT: line 1 is a short hook. Then 2-4 short lines of value taken from the SOURCE. Then one call to action. The last line has 3-5 relevant hashtags. Keep the whole post under 450 characters. Do NOT include any link or URL. Output only the post text."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "45173992-5f58-4f4b-89f4-3b3b3e89daca",
      "name": "Generate Post",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [
        2720,
        672
      ]
    },
    {
